WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.100
The brutal Starz series Spartacus&nbsp;
was known for its highly-stylized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:10.020
gore and its many liberties taken with&nbsp;
historical fact. Lasting four seasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:14.040
it covers one of the greatest rebel&nbsp;
leaders in history, his allies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:18.887
and his many, many foes. Here's what the&nbsp;
cast of the popular show is up to now.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:24.480
Expectations were high for Liam McIntyre when&nbsp;
he stepped in to replace Andy Whitfield as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:29.460
main character of Spartacus, but he arguably did&nbsp;
quite well in the titular role. While certainly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.480
different from Whitfield, McIntyre's turn as&nbsp;
Spartacus took the character from a gladiator&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:38.760
slave to a freedom fighter commander — remaining&nbsp;
one of his most famous roles to this day.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:46.020
"Spread word to every slave yet beneath heel that&nbsp;
even the mighty Republic bleeds when struck!"

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.520
In the years since, McIntyre has been quite busy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:55.620
both in his career and family life. From&nbsp;
appearing in major TV shows like The Flash,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:01.320
to providing the voice of JD Fenix in the Gears&nbsp;
of War video game series. In June of 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:06.014
he and his wife Erin announced on social media&nbsp;
that they are expecting their second child.

00:01:06.247 --> 00:01:11.880
Lucy Lawless' Lucretia is one of the early&nbsp;
villains of Spartacus, and the prequel season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:17.520
Gods of the Arena. Her unexpected return in&nbsp;
Season 2 was a welcome surprise for many fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.600
both of Lawless as an actress, and&nbsp;
of her ruthless Roman aristocrat.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.760
Since her days as the titular heroine in Xena:&nbsp;
Warrior Princess, Lawless has been a major player&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:33.120
in both TV and film. Since Spartacus, she's been&nbsp;
a cast member in series such as Salem and Ash vs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:38.400
Evil Dead. Currently, Lawless stars in My Life is&nbsp;
Murder as the private investigator Alexa Crowe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:43.609
and provided the voice of Nun-Chuck in the&nbsp;
2022 animated film, Minions: The Rise of Gru.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:49.200
Even though John Hannah's cruelly ambitious&nbsp;
Batiatus didn't last long on Spartacus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:53.400
he is considered a superb early&nbsp;
antagonist. While viewers can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.560
often feel sympathy for the character's plights,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.560 --> 00:02:01.134
those sentiments are repeatedly dashed upon&nbsp;
seeing how manipulative and cunning Batiatus is.

00:02:01.134 --> 00:02:06.654
"It has taken years and the price of blood,&nbsp;
but I at last see you for what you are.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.720
A man that holds no one in esteem beyond himself."

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:15.960
Hannah has appeared in television and movies&nbsp;
since the early 1990s, with his most memorable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:20.280
role being Jonathan Carnahan, the comic&nbsp;
relief in the Mummy franchise. Hannah&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:25.260
remains incredibly active on screen, starring as&nbsp;
Dr. Jed Bishop in the ongoing series Transplant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:29.760
and appearing in shows like Dirk Gently's&nbsp;
Holistic Detective Agency and The Victim.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:34.680
In a show littered with tragic endings&nbsp;
for most of the central characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:40.200
Crixus — the dependable rival-turned-ally of&nbsp;
Spartacus, portrayed by Manu Bennett — also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:44.820
meets a grim fate. But Bennett had a fantastic&nbsp;
run with the character up until that point.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:49.860
Bennett has had many major credits in the&nbsp;
years since Spartacus. Perhaps best known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:52.560
for playing Deathstroke in the CW series Arrow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:57.360
and Azog in Peter Jackson's The Hobbit trilogy.&nbsp;
Recently, Bennett posted on Instagram that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.100
considers one of the most important roles&nbsp;
of his career being in the 2022 film Muru,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:06.720
which spotlighted the controversial terror&nbsp;
raids carried out in 2007 by New Zealand police.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.840
The actor admitted that he was&nbsp;
initially hesitant to take on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:13.500
the role of the oppressor. But after a&nbsp;
heart-to-heart with the lead star — Cliff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:17.700
Curtis — he was convinced to take the&nbsp;
part. Bennett told the Otago Daily Times,

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:22.620
"They say a hero is only as strong as their&nbsp;
villain, or a protagonist is only as strong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:27.288
as the antagonist. You have to bring that&nbsp;
energy out, and that's my job as an actor."

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:32.820
Many fans consider Peter Mensah's turn as the&nbsp;
stern and stoic Oenomaus a formidable presence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:37.860
in Spartacus. Oenomaus is critical, not only&nbsp;
for training Spartacus and the other gladiators,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:41.100
but for also becoming a key part&nbsp;
of the revolt against the Romans.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:45.420
"Is this not enough? How many more must die?"

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:47.662
"I would see but one."

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.440
Mensah has often featured in shows and movies&nbsp;
with high levels of tension and action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:57.780
and that trend continues to this day. The&nbsp;
actor is set to star as Governor Gaddo in Rise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:02.340
a thriller centered on a Nigerian princess'&nbsp;
desperate mission to save her sister from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:07.980
clutches of Boko Haram. Mensah has also delivered&nbsp;
heart-pounding performances in the 2022 horror&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:13.620
films Hypochondriac and The Devil Conspiracy,&nbsp;
and played the Blind Master in the 2021 movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:17.220
Snake Eyes — the latest installment&nbsp;
of the G.I. Joe film franchise.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:20.820
Mensah has also continued working&nbsp;
for the small screen since Spartacus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:23.460
with his credits including&nbsp;
series like Sleepy Hollow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:27.273
as well as playing the villainous Qovas&nbsp;
in Marvel's Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:04:27.429 --> 00:04:31.080
Daniel Feuerriegel's Agron&nbsp;
is one of Spartacus's most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:35.100
trusted lieutenants. Even though he&nbsp;
is surrounded by doomed characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:40.200
and even witnesses the heartbreaking murder of&nbsp;
his brother Duro at the hands of a Roman guard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:44.580
Agron is one of the few rebels who&nbsp;
survives to the end of the series.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.740
In the years since the end of Spartacus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:51.060
Feuerriegel took on the role of EJ DiMera in&nbsp;
the popular soap opera, Days of Our Lives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:55.800
and appeared in films like Pacific Rim: Uprising,&nbsp;
and the upcoming Heidi: Queen of the Mountain.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:01.020
Outside of films and TV, Feuerriegel has also&nbsp;
been busy publishing his own graphic novel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:03.360
Fractured Shards, telling TV Insider,

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:07.500
"It's been an absolute blast. It's&nbsp;
been phenomenal. You pitch the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.720
you write it, and then you see the artist and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:13.260
colorist do their things [...] It's&nbsp;
such a fun collaborative effort."

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:19.020
To say that Nick E. Tarabay's character,&nbsp;
Ashur, is "sneaky" would certainly be an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:22.500
understatement. First as a slave and then&nbsp;
as the willing servant of the Romans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:27.240
Ashur does whatever it takes to survive,&nbsp;
which includes stabbing anyone who gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:31.140
in his way in the back. Yet in the&nbsp;
end, the traitor reaps what he sows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:35.040
and is slain by the former slave Naevia&nbsp;
for his horrible crimes against her.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:39.900
"I will have his life for what he did to me!"

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:44.520
Following the end of the Starz series,&nbsp;
Tarabay had a prominent role as Cotyar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:48.900
in the sci-fi series The Expanse, as well&nbsp;
as smaller roles in series like Arrow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:53.820
and Motherland: Fort Salem. More recently, the&nbsp;
actor has appeared in The Cleaning Lady in 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:58.860
as well as taking on the recurring part of Eclipso&nbsp;
in the DC series Stargirl. Tarabay's voice can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:03.600
also be heard in video games like BioWare's&nbsp;
Anthem, and The Dark Pictures: House of Ashes.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:09.240
The whole Spartacus saga began when our titular&nbsp;
hero was forcefully separated from his lover,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:13.680
Sura. This tragic romance made it difficult&nbsp;
for actress Katrina Law to enter the series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:18.420
as the "new woman" in Spartacus' life —&nbsp;
the slave-turned-warrior, Mira. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:22.680
throughout the series, Mira becomes much more&nbsp;
than just the protagonist's lover — playing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:25.560
pivotal role supporting the revolt&nbsp;
leader in their fight for freedom.

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:30.840
Following her work on the Starz action drama,&nbsp;
Law has continued a prolific career in film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:35.700
and television. Her most recognizable role&nbsp;
in recent years is arguably that of special&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:41.160
agent Jessica Knight in NCIS and NCIS: Hawai'i,&nbsp;
but she's also had other major parts like Karen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:46.478
Beach in the thriller series The Oath, and&nbsp;
the formidable Nyssa al Ghul in DC's Arrow.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:51.360
While Liam McIntyre replacing Andy Whitfield&nbsp;
wasn't the only actor swap to take the place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:55.140
on Spartacus, Cynthia Addai-Robinson&nbsp;
stepping in for Lesley-Ann Brandt to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:58.740
play Naevia for the 2012 Vengeance&nbsp;
season was for altogether different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:03.360
reasons — with Brandt choosing to leave due&nbsp;
to scheduling conflicts and production delays.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:08.100
The character Naevia had endured horrific&nbsp;
treatment as a slave in the Roman mines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:13.380
and her transformation into a fearless warrior&nbsp;
is fiercely performed by Addai-Robinson.

00:07:13.816 --> 00:07:21.916
"There is but single reason Crassus spared my&nbsp;
life. To taunt Spartacus with vision of his end."

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:26.520
Addai-Robinson's other prominent roles&nbsp;
since include Nadine Memphis in the TV&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:30.420
adaptation of Shooter, Ramona Garrity&nbsp;
in the acclaimed crime saga Power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:35.820
and Suicide Squad mastermind Amanda Waller&nbsp;
in the Arrowverse. Though Addai-Robinson's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:41.100
biggest recent role is probably that of Queen&nbsp;
Regent Míriel in Amazon's The Lord of the Rings:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:44.460
The Rings of Power. When describing&nbsp;
the part to Men's Journal, she said,

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:49.560
"It's complicated. A Regent Queen is not fully&nbsp;
in power yet. Essentially, I'm trying to lead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:54.720
my people and decide which direction this society&nbsp;
is going to take. It's a fork-in-the-road moment."

00:07:55.260 --> 00:08:00.840
As Ilithyia, Viva Bianca had a fascinating&nbsp;
role in Spartacus — not just as the wife&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:04.740
of the hero's arch nemesis Glaber,&nbsp;
but also as the possible mother of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:08.280
Spartacus' child. Whether that&nbsp;
last bit is truth or trickery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:12.660
the controversial infant eventually&nbsp;
leads to the Roman noblewoman's downfall.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:17.760
Bianca has appeared in several productions&nbsp;
after Spartacus, including the popular 2015&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:22.200
holiday film, A Prince for Christmas, but she&nbsp;
has scaled back her on-screen acting in more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:26.520
recent years. Instead, focusing on producing&nbsp;
and directing the climate crisis documentary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:31.560
Generation GND. In September of 2022, she&nbsp;
posted on Instagram that she and her family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:36.600
finally settled in a new home after spending&nbsp;
a good amount of time moving around. She said,

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:42.360
"In the last 2.5 years we moved 6 times&nbsp;
[...] across oceans and state lines.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:46.560
That's a lot for anyone but especially a&nbsp;
lot [if] you have little people in tow."

00:08:47.067 --> 00:08:52.380
Craig Parker's Roman commander Gaius Claudius&nbsp;
Glaber, quickly becomes the despised nemesis of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:57.120
Spartacus at the beginning of his turbulent saga.&nbsp;
Whereas Spartacus' other early enemy, Batiatus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:02.160
pretends to be on the titular character's side,&nbsp;
Glaber acts with open arrogance and contempt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:07.129
towards the Thracian — even when reaching out&nbsp;
to fight alongside him as a military ally.

00:09:07.129 --> 00:09:09.060
"I shall take my leave when Spartacus falls."

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:11.040
"A task long overdue in its completion."

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:12.300
"Yet now within grasp."

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:16.980
After Glaber causes Spartacus to lose&nbsp;
everything — including his freedom and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:21.000
his wife, Sura — the rebel leader scores&nbsp;
a major victory in his war against the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:24.840
Romans when he finally gets revenge&nbsp;
in the aptly titled Vengeance season.

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:29.100
Following Spartacus, Parker has appeared&nbsp;
in minor roles in many different TV series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:34.500
including Yuri in the romantic dramedy Good&nbsp;
Trouble and the 2018 revival of Charmed. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:40.680
his biggest roles since Spartacus are arguably as&nbsp;
Stéphane Narcisse in the historical drama Reign,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:45.180
and Guy Warner in the New Zealand soap&nbsp;
opera, Shortland Street. The actor is also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:50.280
cast in the upcoming thriller A Social Contract&nbsp;
alongside Lord of the Rings alumni, Sean Astin.

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:56.100
When the status of Spartacus was uncertain due to&nbsp;
the health concerns of lead star Andy Whitfield,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.100 --> 00:10:00.240
Dustin Clare stepped in to become the main&nbsp;
character, Gannicus, in the prequel season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:05.760
Gods of the Arena. Gannicus was popular enough to&nbsp;
return in later seasons and join the slave revolt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:10.860
against the Romans, using his legendary fighting&nbsp;
skills as a gladiator to devastating effect.

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:15.300
Clare has been a TV star for some time&nbsp;
and continues to feature in many different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:20.040
productions to this day. Most recently, the actor&nbsp;
played a major part in the series Surviving Summer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:25.247
as Thommo Gibson, and the character George&nbsp;
Michael in the 2022 drama film, Seriously Red.

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:30.660
Beginning in Spartacus: Vengeance, actress&nbsp;
Ellen Hollman plays the formidable Germanic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:35.160
warrior Saxa, who joins the slave revolt&nbsp;
after being freed by Spartacus and Agron.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:39.060
As part of the rebel forces, Saxa&nbsp;
fights valiantly and eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:43.740
forms a complicated yet strong bond with&nbsp;
Gannicus, making it all the more painful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:48.025
for the ex-gladiator when she tragically dies&nbsp;
in his arms during a battle with the Romans.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:50.760
The character may have met&nbsp;
a tragic end on Spartacus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:55.740
but the part led Hollman to a substantial&nbsp;
career in both TV and film. She's earned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.740 --> 00:11:01.080
credits on major shows, including Lethal&nbsp;
Weapon, Into the Badlands, NCIS, and NCIS:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:06.294
New Orleans. In film, Hollman recently appeared&nbsp;
in The Matrix Resurrections as the character Echo.

00:11:06.649 --> 00:11:10.260
Nasir — played by Pana Hema Taylor —&nbsp;
is a later addition to the rebel cause,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.260 --> 00:11:14.640
joining the cast in Spartacus: Vengeance.&nbsp;
He quickly becomes one of the rebellion's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:18.180
most ardent supporters, though he&nbsp;
initially has no idea how to fight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:22.440
and even opposes Spartacus. However,&nbsp;
our titular hero chooses to train him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:28.140
and from then on, Nasir is extremely devoted&nbsp;
to the war effort. He is seemingly rewarded by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:32.460
the gods for that devotion, getting to live&nbsp;
his remaining days with his lover, Agron.

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:37.200
Taylor has mostly worked on projects in his&nbsp;
native New Zealand since the end of Spartacus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:42.720
including major roles in Dirty Laundry and The&nbsp;
Brokenwood Mysteries. His most notable role since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:49.440
Nasir may be that of Bert Thompson in Westside —&nbsp;
appearing in 49 episodes of the series since 2015.

